  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs) in Asia and the Pacific have strengthened their institutional capacity to represent and support their members in an increasingly complex business environment. The ILO&#x2019;s continuous support to Asia Pacific EBMOs aims to achieve economies of scale by supporting the adaptation and testing of innovative approaches and sharing of regional best practices and lessons learned. This support also leverages partnership with development cooperations to deliver targeted opportunities for technical and functional capacity through enhanced knowledge, tools and regional collaboration in order to better equip EBMOs in providing evidence-based policy advocacy, respond to emerging trade sustainability and human rights due diligence requirements and support enterprises in adapting to technological and labour market challenges. EBMOs are better positioned to engage in policy discussions on trade, labour standards, migration, environmental, social and governance issues, and responsible business conduct, while leveraging digital technologies, including AI, to improve governance, member services and organizational effectiveness. As a result, EBMOs become stronger, more representative and more influential institutions that contribute to sustainable enterprise development, competitivene3ss and decent work across the region.</narrative>
  </description>
